response.value:
The condition is correct, but `best` never changes. It remains `0`, so every positive score satisfies `best < score`.

When a new best is found, update both the display and the variable:

```js
if (best < score) {
    best = score;
    document.getElementById("bestScore").textContent = best.toString();
}
```

The important line is:

```js
best = score;
```

Then future scores are compared with the actual best score. Also ensure this block runs whenever the game ends.
